{"id":"qsz-92","slug":"qsz-92","name":"QSZ-92","aliases":["QSZ-92 pistol","Norinco QSZ 92"],"kind":"firearm","category":"pistols","subcategory":"Semi-automatic pistol","description":"The QSZ-92, also known as the Type 92 (Chinese: 92式手枪; pinyin: Jiǔ Shì Èr Shoǔqiāng; lit. 'Type 92 Handgun'), is a semi-automatic pistol designed by Norinco.","history":"The decision to develop a new pistol was made in 1987 to replace the Type 54/64/77. Research and development started in 1992.\nDevelopment of the QSZ-92 pistol began in 1994 and was adopted by the People's Liberation Army's forces in 1998. The export variants (9×19mm versions) include the CF-98 (barrel life c. 8,000 rds) and the NP-42 (barrel life c. 10,000 rds). The latter is the basic version without provisions for suppressor etc. Both have so far found commercial export in Canada. The CF-98 has also been sighted in parts of Africa.\nIn June 2022, it's reported that Iraq has made the pistol as the Babylon through the Defence Industries Commission. They are sold to Iraqi lawyers who need personal protection. Former prime minister Mustafa Al-Kadhimi was gifted the first Babylon made. It was reported that Norinco provided assistance in manufacturing the Babylon.\nOn 11 July 2024, it was confirmed that the Hong Kong Police Force would adopt the CF98A and CS/LP5 respectively to replace the S&W M10HB revolvers for uniformed officers and SIG P250 Dcc pistols for detectives as necessary parts for maintenance are running out.","facts":[],"specifications":[{"group":"Cartridge & Action","items":[{"label":"Cartridge","value":"5.8×21mm DAP92"},{"label":"Cartridge","value":"9×19mm Parabellum"},{"label":"Action","value":"Short recoil, locked breech, rotating barrel lock"},{"label":"Muzzle Velocity","value":"350 m/s (1,150 ft/s) (9×19mm Parabellum)","numeric":350,"unit":"m/s"},{"label":"Feed System (Detachable box magazine; capacities)","value":"15 rounds (9×19mm)"},{"label":"Feed System (Detachable box magazine; capacities)","value":"20 rounds (5.8×21mm)"},{"label":"Sights","value":"Fixed, 3-dot type"}]},{"group":"Dimensions","items":[{"label":"Weight","value":"760 g","numeric":760,"unit":"g"},{"label":"Length","value":"190 mm (7.48 in)","numeric":190,"unit":"mm"},{"label":"Barrel Length","value":"111 mm (4.33 in)","numeric":111,"unit":"mm"},{"label":"Width","value":"35 mm","numeric":35,"unit":"mm"},{"label":"Height","value":"135 mm","numeric":135,"unit":"mm"}]},{"group":"Performance","items":[{"label":"Effective Range","value":"50 m (9×19mm Parabellum)","numeric":50,"unit":"m"}]},{"group":"Production","items":[{"label":"Designer","value":"Liu Ming (刘铭) of the Small Arms Research Institute (formerly the 208 Research Institute); also attributed to Qing Shangsheng (卿上升)"},{"label":"Designed","value":"early 1990s"},{"label":"Manufacturer","value":"Chongqing Changfeng Machine Manufacturing Ltd"},{"label":"Produced","value":"1998–present"}]},{"group":"Service","items":[{"label":"Origin","value":"China"}]}],"specIndex":{"Cartridge":"5.8×21mm DAP92","Action":"Short recoil, locked breech, rotating barrel lock","Muzzle Velocity":"350 m/s (1,150 ft/s) (9×19mm Parabellum)","Feed System":"15 rounds (9×19mm)","Sights":"Fixed, 3-dot type","Weight":"760 g","Length":"190 mm (7.48 in)","Barrel Length":"111 mm (4.33 in)","Width":"35 mm","Height":"135 mm","Effective Range":"50 m (9×19mm Parabellum)","Designer":"Liu Ming (刘铭) of the Small Arms Research Institute (formerly the 208 Research Institute); also attributed to Qing Shangsheng (卿上升)","Designed":"early 1990s","Manufacturer":"Chongqing Changfeng Machine Manufacturing Ltd","Produced":"1998–present","Origin":"China"},"images":{"hero":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/43/QSZ92_-_5.8mm_Pistol_20170919.jpg","descriptionUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:QSZ92_-_5.8mm_Pistol_20170919.jpg","width":2400,"height":1800,"license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","attribution":"Tyg728"},"thum